Thylacine: force SDL's dummy audio driver so SDL_Init does not E_Exit.

DOSBox-X's main SDL bring-up calls SDL_Init(SDL_INIT_AUDIO|SDL_INIT_VIDEO|
SDL_INIT_TIMER|...) as one combined call and treats any failure as fatal
(E_Exit "Can't init SDL ..."). Thylacine ships no SDL audio backend (sound
is a v1.0 non-goal), so every real audio driver fails and the combined init
aborts with "No available audio device" before the video surface is ever
created. SDL's dummy audio driver is compiled in but demand-only (never an
auto-fallback), so setenv SDL_AUDIODRIVER=dummy (overwrite=0, respecting an
explicit choice) makes SDL_INIT_AUDIO succeed silently and lets the render
path run. Guarded by __thylacine__ so upstream and other targets are untouched.
--- a/src/gui/sdlmain.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/sdlmain.cpp
@@ -9504,6 +9504,14 @@
 	CheckPreventCap();
 	LOG_MSG("Prevent capture: %u",preventcap);
 
+#if defined(__thylacine__)
+        /* Thylacine ships no SDL audio backend (sound is a v1.0 non-goal), so
+         * every real audio driver fails and the combined SDL_Init below would
+         * abort on SDL_INIT_AUDIO with "No available audio device" -> E_Exit.
+         * Force SDL's demand-only dummy driver so audio inits silently;
+         * overwrite=0 respects an explicit SDL_AUDIODRIVER. */
+        setenv("SDL_AUDIODRIVER", "dummy", 0);
+#endif
         /* -- SDL init */
         if (SDL_Init(SDL_INIT_AUDIO|SDL_INIT_VIDEO|SDL_INIT_TIMER|SDL_INIT_NOPARACHUTE) >= 0)
             sdl.inited = true;
